# Line-ending normalisation.
#
# This repo is worked on from both Windows and macOS. Without this file the two
# machines committed the same content with different line endings, which showed up
# as whole-file diffs on cap.obj / lens.obj / cap_membrane.py and hid the real
# changes. Worse, run_cap.sh once got committed with CRLF, which makes macOS bash
# fail with "/bin/bash^M: bad interpreter".
#
# text=auto  -> git detects text vs binary (PDFs in papers/ stay untouched)
# eol=lf     -> text files are stored AND checked out as LF on every platform
* text=auto eol=lf

# PowerShell and batch scripts stay CRLF: that is what the Windows tooling expects.
*.ps1 text eol=crlf
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf
